    "media:imagetext": "HAROLD MC MILLAN BIXBY\nBOLTON LANDING, N. Y.\nOct. 5th\nDear Emmy Lu:\nYours of the lst. I have advised the Foundation that I shall not\nattend the meeting in Omaha in November.\nDo you think you might\nperhaps build a small fire under our Tallahassee politicos by send-\ning them the agenda for the Omaha meeting withthe suggestion that\nthey may perhaps miss\nthe bus by reason of their activity on the\ndo nothing frontier.\nI think Evans might be the one to call the\nGovernor's attention to the fact that the Darling Foundation tired\nof waiting for action in Florida is turning its attention toward\nthe Lewis and Clark promotion. I frankly do not know whether or\nnot that would do any good.\nDebby and I have postponed our trip and now plan on going down to\nNew York on or about the 21st as I have a meeting to attend on the\nI had hoped to spend a little time in N.Y. but apart from the\nmeeting on the 23rd there is nothing to keep me there. Could you\nconveniently set up the meeting in Tallahassee for a day or two\nlater than the 25th date that you suggest in your letter? I could\nmake it on the 25th if I have to but would prefer a few days later.\nIn any event Debby will stay on in N.Y. while I go on to Tallahassee\nand Captiva. We are having our car driven down so we are quite flex-\nible.\nTried to phone you tonight but no answer. Guess this letter will do\nas well because we have lots of time.\nlf you should wish to reach\nme our number is Bolton Landing NH 4 9765.\nRemember that I can be\nin Tallahassee on the 25th if required and I quite agree that we can\naccomplish something if we meet\nthere in force.\nIn fact I do not\nbelieve a darn thing will happen unless and until we do.\nGive Mary and Dick my very best when you see them.\nSincerely",
